WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.434
-Holy moly!
Whoa! Whoa!

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.767
It is so great to be here!
Wow!

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.767
I feel -- I feel so light.
I feel free.

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:09.267
It's like --
It's like I just

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.334
took my weighted blanket off,
you know?

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.901
[ Laughter ]
Hoo!

00:00:12.901 --> 00:00:14.901
I love the weighted blanket.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.367
I don't know if you guys are
into that, but, oh, man.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.934
It's a blanket
that literally depresses you.

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:21.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:23.100
It's so nice
to have something to blame

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.634
for why you can't get up.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.434
This blanket just holds you
in place, holds you down.

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:29.968
It goes,
"It's my fault tonight,"

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.634
and you go,
"Thank you, blanket."

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.667
They say
you're supposed to calculate

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.601
10% of your body weight.

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.701
That's how heavy
your blanket's supposed to be.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:42.300
But I didn't do the math.
I know myself.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.501
I have the depression
of a much larger person,

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:48.734
and I want to get crushed, okay?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:51.234
I want to feel like the bed's
sleeping on me.

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:52.667
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:55.701
I got a 20-pounder.
Not to brag, but...

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.567
It's good.
I used to go to the gym

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:01.434
and lift 20-pound weights.
Now I just wait

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:04.133
until I have to pee
and fight the blanket off of me.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.801
You don't get laid
under a weighted blanket.

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:12.934
[ Laughter ]
You all knew that.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.934
Just a little
public-service announcement.

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.167
I don't know
if there's anyone here

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:21.200
who has both a weighted blanket
and a partner.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.801
Might be kind of a small center
of the Venn diagram, but...

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:28.934
You gotta try, you know?
I try.

00:01:28.934 --> 00:01:30.868
My fiancé comes home,
and I'm like,

00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.601
"Peel the sandbag off of me."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.501
"Don't you want to see
what kind of corpse

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:39.434
is steaming under here?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:41.501
It's a pretty tough sell,
you know?

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.601
'Cause even if he wanted to take
the weighted blanket off me,

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.133
he'd still have to get
the night guard out of my mouth.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:48.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.033
It's a whole process, you know?

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:52.734
It's a striptease.
That's what I'm doing.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:56.133
The weighted blanket comes off,
the night guard pops out,

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:59.267
you take off the eye mask,
you take out the ear plugs,

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:01.334
you take off the snore strip --
rip!

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:03.634
You leave the humidifier on.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.067
[ Laughter and applause ]
Yeah!

00:02:05.067 --> 00:02:07.934
'Cause you don't
want to get dry.

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:09.767
Right, fellas?
Okay.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.734
Do we have any
night-guard wearers here?

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.167
[ Cheers ]
Yeah?

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.934
Are you clenching,
or are you grinding?

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:21.033
-Both!
-Both! Me, too!

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:23.501
We're furious!
Isn't that fun?

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:24.801
[ Laughter ]
Oh, man.

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.400
If you don't know what
a night guard is,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.868
it's kind of like the
mouth piece you wear for hockey

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:32.267
if the hockey's in your mind.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.033
And it's good.
You know?

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.100
It does the job,
'cause that anger

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.634
has got to go somewhere,
you know?

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.267
I want to be nice
during the day,

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:42.300
so I just take all my anger out
on myself in my sleep.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.367
[ Laughter ]
That's what I do.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.667
I start my days.
I'm like, "Good morning!

00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.133
I love you.
I love meetings.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.167
I love when men talk over me
in meetings.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:54.067
Yes, I said it first,
but you said it taller."

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.634
And then,
at the end of the day, you know,

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.734
go home, go to sleep,
put in the night guard,

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:03.167
and just grind it out.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.667
As soon as I'm asleep, I'm like,

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:07.834
"I will destroy myself
in my rest!"

00:03:07.834 --> 00:03:10.367
And then wake up and go,
"Good morning!

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:13.200
I love you.
I have a headache."

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.000
It's healthy.
It's wellness.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.934
I do feel so blindsided

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:22.100
by the number
of sleep accessories I require.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.133
It's more than I thought,
you know?

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:27.534
I didn't think I'd grow up
and have to gear up for sleep.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:28.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:30.200
I wish someone had warned me.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:34.434
I wish when I was a kid, there'd
been a Sleep Disorder Barbie.

00:03:34.434 --> 00:03:36.534
You know, just to get
the image in your head, right?

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.601
Just to see little girls
being like,

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:42.200
"My Barbie likes melatonin!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:45.200
"My Barbie smokes weed
till she's tired."

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.334
"Whoa! Ken sleeps
in a separate bedroom!"

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:50.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.601
Thank you, guys, so much.
I'm Emmy Blotnick.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:53.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

